    "title": "Local man jailed for lobster poaching - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n4 hours ago\nISLAMORADA — A 28-year-old local man has been sentenced to 100 days in jail after being caught with large quantity of illegally harvested spiny lobster and other out-of-season species in Monroe County waters.\nOn Aug. 3, officers with the Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission (FWC), assisted by the Monroe County Sheriff’s Office, arrested Marcos Hernandez Gregorio after observing him in the water near Indian Key Fill with equipment commonly associated with lobster harvesting, despite the fact that lobster season was closed, reports say.\nUpon inspection, officers discovered he was in possession of multiple undersized lobsters, along with other species taken out of season and by illegal methods, reports say.\nOn Aug. 20, Hernandez Gregorio pleaded no contest before County Judge Sharon Hamilton and was adjudicated guilty on all charges. In addition to his jail sentence, he was ordered to pay court costs and fines.\n“This was a deliberate violation of Florida’s fishery laws,” State Attorney Dennis Ward said. “FWC and the Monroe County Sheriff’s Office acted quickly to protect our marine resources, which are vital to our environment and economy.”",
